Section 6: Responsible AI Requirements

This is where Responsible AI lives.

Require:

Human Oversight

How are humans involved? - Box AI requires human oversight to prevent harm, especially in high-risk decision-making. Customers are responsible for combining human judgment with AI-generated insights rather than relying entirely on automated outputs, and they must avoid using Box AI for consequential decisions—such as employment, healthcare, or legal matters—without explicit human review.

Transparency

How are users informed AI is being used? - Box AI informs users about AI usage through disclosure statements and transparency labeling practices aligned with industry standards, ensuring users understand when they are interacting with AI systems rather than human-generated content or processes.

Accountability

Who owns outcomes? - The deploying organization bears primary accountability for operational outcomes of Box AI systems, including agent behavior, decision-making authority, and performance results. This accountability extends to how the organization defines scope, authorizes autonomy levels, and oversees live operations—not to platform operators, integrators, or model providers.

Fairness

How will bias be managed? - Box AI manages bias through rigorous model evaluation, continuous testing across diverse use cases, and customer responsibility frameworks that emphasize human oversight and awareness of inherent AI limitations.

Privacy

How will sensitive data be protected? - Box AI protects sensitive data through layered security controls, permission-based access restrictions, and explicit data governance policies that prevent unauthorized exposure while maintaining customer control over content processing.

Security

How will access and usage be secured? - Box AI secures access and usage through permissions-aware architecture, OAuth authentication, and granular administrative controls that enforce existing Box security policies across all AI interactions while preventing unauthorized content exposure.

